  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\nThe [CSS Cascading and Inheritance Level 6 spec](https://www.w3.org/TR/css-cascade-6/#example-52419898) uses the following example code when explaining `@scope`:\n\n```html\n<div>\n  <style>\n    @scope {\n      p { color: red; }\n    }\n  </style>\n  <p>this is red</p>\n</div>\n<p>not red</p>\n```\n\nThis code works in all browsers but conformance checkers like https://checker.html5.org/ will flag use of `<style>` inside of the `<body>` as invalid. The validity should be reconsidered.\n\nThis issue was previously [discussed here](https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/1605).",
